(Ord. of 9-28-1993(1), § 3)

661:
It shall be the duty of each dealer liable for the tax imposed by this article to report, on or before the 20th day of each calendar month, to the board of county commissioners on forms furnished by the county, or on forms prepared by the reporting taxpayer and disclosing the same information:
(1) The number of rooms, or other units of accommodation furnished during the preceding calendar month and the total charges therefor (excluding charges for telephone, food and beverage services, if any);
(2) The number of rooms or other units of accommodation furnished to the same occupant for a period exceeding ten consecutive days; and the total charges therefor (excluding charges for telephone, food and beverage services, if any);
(3) The tax base;
(4) The total tax due for the month preceding the month of filing; and
(5) Any such other information as may be required by the board of commissioners.
All such reports shall be made under oath and shall be signed by the reporting dealer.
(Ord. of 11-14-1978, § 5)

